The brute force approach is just checking all the possible combinations.
the most optimal approach is making a hashmap and an integer that tell how much more should be added to the current element to get
to the target after this we search if the map consists of the more element return the index of the more element and the current element
if not add the current element to the map for future usecase.
code--
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> twoSum(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        unordered_map<int,int>mpp;
        for(int i =0;i<nums.size();i++){
            int more = target-nums[i] ;
            if(mpp.find(more)!=mpp.end()){
                return {mpp[more],i};
            }
            mpp[nums[i]] = i;
        }
        return {};
    }
};
time complexity-- O(n)
